TI  - Usability of Virtual Reality Based Bathroom Safety Education System for Dementia 
      Caregiver: A Nielsen Heuristics Approach.
PG  - 2006-2007
LID - 10.3233/SHTI251322 [doi]
AB  - Falls in bathrooms pose a significant health risk for the elderly, particularly 
      those with dementia. This study developed a Virtual Reality based bathroom safety 
      application for dementia caregivers and evaluated its usability to enhance 
      learning outcomes. Thirteen hazardous items identified by expert nurses were 
      integrated into the virtual environment, and User Interface/User experience 
      design improvements were made based on Nielsen's heuristics. Experimental results 
      showed that both the experimental and control groups exceeded the usability 
      benchmark score of 68 on the System Usability Scale, with identical quiz accuracy 
      rates of 88.33%. Interviews with the control group highlighted features 
      implemented in the experimental group, suggesting that the user-centered design 
      improved usability and can enhance learning outcomes with iterations.
