TI  - [Virtual reality reminiscence intervention for elderly people with cognitive and 
      mood disorders].
PG  - 15-20
LID - S1268-6034(25)00022-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.sger.2025.02.004 [doi]
AB  - The study examines the impact of personalized virtual reality (VR) on mood 
      disorders in elderly people with neurocognitive disorders (NCD) living in nursing 
      homes and long-term care units. Twenty-seven participants were divided into two 
      groups ("personalized" versus "generic") and underwent twelve immersive VR 
      sessions. Results showed an improvement in mood disorders and quality of life, 
      with no significant difference between groups. Future research is needed on the 
      use of VR in non-drug interventions.
