TI  - Executive functions in a virtual world: a study in Parkinson's disease.
PG  - 92-6
AB  - In Parkinson's disease executive functions are altered. We used a Virtual Reality 
      version of the Multiple Errand Test in order to evaluate decision-making ability 
      in 12 patients and 14 controls. Patients with Parkinson's disease, even if 
      not-demented, showed strategies full of errors, suggesting that impulse control 
      disorder, very frequent in course of disease, could precede cognitive 
      dysfunctions.
