TI  - Serious games for screening pre-dementia conditions: from virtuality to reality? 
      A pilot project.
PG  - 153-8
AB  - Conventional cognitive assessment is based on a pencil-and-paper 
      neuropsychological evaluation, which is time consuming, expensive and requires 
      the involvement of several professionals. Information and communication 
      technology could be exploited to allow the development of tools that are easy to 
      use, reduce the amount of data processing, and provide controllable test 
      conditions. Serious games (SGs) have the potential to be new and effective tools 
      in the management and treatment of cognitive impairments Serious games for 
      screening pre-dementia conditions: from virtuality to reality? A pilot project in 
      the elderly. Moreover, by adopting SGs in 3D virtual reality settings, cognitive 
      functions might be evaluated using tasks that simulate daily activities, 
      increasing the "ecological validity" of the assessment. In this commentary we 
      report our experience in the creation of the Smart Aging platform, a 3D SGand 
      virtual environment-based platform for the early identification and 
      characterization of mild cognitive impairment.
